"},{"content_hash":"61b36fa39d4e2fe23fb3ae7c0a7134c6586fe7c0c866ae44dfc980c796981faf","event_uuid":"17a5b931-dc64-4c2b-a8e1-4fa8fce0241d","position":{"commit_sha":"959fda2aa4364d8eb5b914906f37c853b21604be","position":"1786498901135120001-17a5b931-dc64-4c2b-a8e1-4fa8fce0241d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"2c0eef4153bcb147c59a7ffd18ea36da4cc28e62a1fbe2bc84636bea6b3773d4","event_uuid":"326a2af5-f07c-463b-b30e-d77686d305fc","position":{"commit_sha":"959fda2aa4364d8eb5b914906f37c853b21604be","position":"1786498901842051001-326a2af5-f07c-463b-b30e-d77686d305fc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[],"created_at":1785864420139764001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"439b1d07-e017-45bd-a981-27bd9b995f1b","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3e73-72b5-cff2-40f0"},{"link_uuid":"d507ac28-d086-4f25-9dbc-4fb9c7dc1af4","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb"},{"link_uuid":"9b7eb90f-f77b-4290-a863-03611b77ec1d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e369-a449-4773-48fb"}],"description":"Discovered during the DC<->Cloud test-parity re-audit (epic 3e73-72b5-cff2-40f0).\n\nDC pins the empty-outbound-assignee behaviour POSITIVELY:\n`tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_unassign_751e.py::test_empty_outbound_assignee_actually_unassigns`\nand `::test_unassign_co_submitted_with_an_editable_field_does_both`.\n\nCloud has the implementation (bug 85a1, `AcliClient.update_issue` in\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli.py`: an assignee in `(None, \"\")` is POPPED and\nrouted to `self.unassign_issue(...)` instead of being sent to ACLI as `--assignee \"\"`, which ACLI\nsilently no-ops), but the only Cloud test is NEGATIVE\n(`mutate/test_assignee_validation.py::test_update_issue_transient_error_propagates_does_not_unassign`).\nNothing asserts the positive path, so a regression that re-forwards `--assignee \"\"` — the exact\nsilent-success defect 85a1 fixed — would keep every Cloud test green.\n\nScope: TEST-ONLY. Behaviour-preserving; no production file is modified. The new test drives the real\n`AcliClient.update_issue` with `unassign_issue` recorded on a fake and `acli_subprocess._run_acli`\nstubbed (deterministic, no subprocess, no network).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] New file `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_cloud_unassign_6a74.py` exists and contains the\n      Cloud characterization, with a docstring naming the DC tests it mirrors.\n- [ ] A test asserts that `AcliClient.update_issue(key, assignee=\"\")` calls `unassign_issue(key)`\n      exactly once AND spawns no `workitem edit` subprocess (no editable field remains).\n- [ ] The same assertion holds for `assignee=None` (both empty sentinels are covered).\n- [ ] A test asserts the co-submit case: `update_issue(key, assignee=\"\", summary=\"new summary\")`\n      calls `unassign_issue(key)` once AND emits a `workitem edit` argv carrying `--summary\n      \"new summary\"` and NO `--assignee` flag — i.e. both halves apply and the empty string never\n      reaches ACLI.\n- [ ] A contrast test asserts a NON-empty assignee still takes the validate-then-edit path:\n      `unassign_issue` is not called and `--assignee` IS present in the argv.\n- [ ] No file under `src/` changes (verified: `git diff --stat` touches only `tests/`).\n\n## Testing\n\n- [ ] Proof: `python -m pytest tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_cloud_unassign_6a74.py -q` passes.\n- [ ] Proof: `make lint` and `make typecheck` pass from the worktree venv.\n- [ ] Proof: the characterization is falsifiable — checked by temporarily removing the empty-assignee\n      branch locally and confirming the new tests FAIL, then reverting.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_cloud_unassign_6a74.py","reason":"New Cloud characterization pinning that an empty/None outbound assignee routes to unassign_issue and co-submits with an editable field (test-only)."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","e369-a449-4773-48fb"],["relates_to","e369-a449-4773-48fb"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"","parent_status_uuid":"17a5b931-dc64-4c2b-a8e1-4fa8fce0241d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"6a74-f464-4ce1-4b79","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Cloud empty-assignee unassign characterization (positive parity with DC test_dc_unassign_751e)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["1516a9ba-9d23-4f8f-9c98-6894c5037e6e","439b1d07-e017-45bd-a981-27bd9b995f1b","d507ac28-d086-4f25-9dbc-4fb9c7dc1af4","51287164-a5e3-4011-a114-6d49cbde8315","386f9f3e-e5f8-4d18-9fc0-fdf738323a12","9b7eb90f-f77b-4290-a863-03611b77ec1d","98358123-08ba-4130-91b5-2b09aca1045d","2366e12d-73ac-4226-8e8e-24df449450a6","dd323943-beeb-4379-aa73-a1a7185f47d8","02475418-0aad-43f7-a7a7-a185bb6b3f9d","7094e1d3-4eec-4b1a-9acf-dcd90ff99e2c","17a5b931-dc64-4c2b-a8e1-4fa8fce0241d","326a2af5-f07c-463b-b30e-d77686d305fc"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786498901842051002,"uuid":"c14b9b21-c2ca-40da-8d4d-5dd852193b98"}